@startuml architecture
title paddock: component architecture

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center

actor User

package "Herdr 0.8.0" {
  [Keybinding\nprefix+c -> popup\n(written by `paddock init`)] as Keybinding
  [herdr CLI\ntab create / pane run] as HerdrCLI
  [Workspace / tabs / panes] as HerdrUI
}

package "paddock" {
  [cli.py\nchoose | launch | attach | profiles | init\n~--cwd, ~--dry-run] as CLI
  [init.py\nsplice the keybinding into\n$HOME/.config/herdr/config.toml\n~--dry-run, ~--undo] as Init
  [tui.py\nquestionary chooser\nanswers -> a plan] as TUI
  [sessions.py\nsession registry\ncreate | attach | remove_pane] as Sessions
  [profiles.py\nProfile dataclass\nnetwork presets] as Profiles
  [agents.py\nagent registry\n+ layer-2 adapters] as Agents
  [synth_config.py\nsynthesized config dir\n(credentials + ticked skills\n+ MCP whitelist)] as SynthConfig
  interface "Backend\nprepare(profile) -> run\nload_run(run_dir) -> run\nopen_pane(run, label)\n-> pane id" as BackendAPI
  [sessions.BACKENDS\nbackend name -> module\n{"srt": backends/srt.py}] as BackendRegistry
  [backends/srt.py\nv1\nbuild_settings / build_shim_dir\npane_command / prepare / open_pane] as SrtBackend
  [backends/microsandbox.py\nv1.1 (planned)] as MsbBackend
  [herdr_client.py\ncreate_tab / run_in_pane\ncheck_config / reload_config\n(mockable seam)] as HerdrClient
}

package "Host configuration" {
  database "~/.config/paddock/\n(override: $PADDOCK_CONFIG_DIR)\nprofiles/*.json\nagents/*.json" as ConfigFiles
  database "~/.local/state/paddock/\n(override: $PADDOCK_STATE_DIR)\nruns/<id>/ bin/ + srt-settings.json +\nconfig/ + work/ + launch.json + launch.sh\nsessions.json (registry: backend, run_dir,\npane ids per session)\nworkspace default bindings (planned)" as RunDir
}

package "Sandbox runtimes" {
  [srt\nSeatbelt (macOS)\nbubblewrap (Linux)] as Srt
  [msb\nlibkrun microVM\nOCI images] as Msb
}

User --> CLI : runs `paddock init` once, after installing
CLI --> Init : init (backs the config up first)
Init --> Keybinding : writes the popup block\nand moves new_tab to prefix+shift+c
Init --> HerdrClient : herdr config check, then reload-config\n(a refused config is put back;\nno herdr to ask is only a message)
User --> Keybinding : presses prefix+c
Keybinding --> CLI : popup runs `paddock`\n(HERDR_SOCKET_PATH,\nHERDR_ACTIVE_WORKSPACE_ID,\nHERDR_ACTIVE_PANE_ID)
CLI --> TUI : choose (default)
TUI --> CLI : one plan:\nlocal | attach | new session
TUI --> Profiles : load / save profile
TUI --> Agents : list agents, remember a typed command
TUI --> Sessions : list live sessions
Sessions ..> RunDir : registry survives\nHerdr restart
Profiles ..> ConfigFiles : reads / writes
Agents ..> ConfigFiles : reads user agents/*.json

CLI --> Sessions : launch_local | get_session + attach | launch\n(the only module that carries a plan out)
BackendAPI <|.. SrtBackend
BackendAPI <|.. MsbBackend

SrtBackend --> RunDir : writes PATH shim dir, srt-settings.json,\nconfig dir, scratch workdir, launch.json, launch.sh
Sessions --> BackendRegistry : backend_for(session.backend):\nprepare on create,\nload_run + open_pane on attach
BackendRegistry --> SrtBackend : "srt"
BackendRegistry ..> MsbBackend : "microsandbox"
Sessions --> HerdrClient : launch_local: a plain tab,\nno session, no sandbox
SrtBackend ..> SynthConfig : build config dir
MsbBackend ..> SynthConfig : build config dir (skills copied:\na host skill path is outside the mount)
Agents --> SynthConfig : credentials + whitelisted skills

SrtBackend --> HerdrClient : pane command + env
MsbBackend ..> HerdrClient : pane command
HerdrClient --> HerdrCLI : herdr tab create [~--workspace] ~--cwd ~--label\n[~--env KEY=VALUE ...] ~--focus\nherdr pane run <pane_id> `exec /bin/sh <run_dir>/launch.sh`\nherdr config check | herdr server reload-config
HerdrCLI --> HerdrUI : creates tab, returns\nresult.root_pane.pane_id
HerdrUI --> Srt : sandboxed pane process (v1)
HerdrUI ..> Msb : sandboxed pane process (v1.1)

note right of BackendAPI
  A backend works the whole launch out as
  plain functions, then opens the pane through
  herdr_client. That client is the seam every
  test mocks, so CI needs no herdr and no srt.

  Each session record names its backend.
  A name that is not in sessions.BACKENDS
  fails at attach with a message; the
  registry still loads.
end note

note bottom of HerdrClient
  The only module that shells out to `herdr`.
  Mocked in every test; CI has no herdr server.
end note

@enduml
